    'rules_en' => <<<'TXT'
1. Joining this somiti is conditional on this first rule: no member may take a personal loan from the somiti's fund.
2. For two (2) years from the month of joining, a member may not cancel their membership at will. A member who wishes to cancel may do so after two (2) years of membership. If membership is cancelled within the two (2) years, the deposited money will be paid only after the two (2) years are complete.
3. The monthly deposit fixed for the number of shares held must be paid between the 1st and the 15th of each month, as scheduled.
4. If a monthly deposit is paid after the scheduled time, a fine of 25 (twenty-five) taka per share per month must be paid.
5. For as many months as an overdue monthly deposit remains unpaid, the fine at the fixed rate must be paid for that many months. An overdue deposit is carried into the next month's account and counts as overdue until it is paid.
6. If a member's monthly deposits are overdue for 6 (six) months, the somiti has the power to cancel that member's membership, based on discussion and agreement of all the other members.
7. All members' deposits, dues, fines, all financial transactions and all financial activities of the somiti will be recorded in the software.
8. All financial transactions of the somiti will be recorded and kept in the software, and the accounts kept in the software will be treated as the final accounts.
9. Through the software, every member can see their own deposited money, all expenses of the somiti, the somiti's total deposits, the somiti's investments, and the income and expense accounts from those investments.
10. Every month, a meeting of members will be held on the somiti's income and expenses and its overall financial activities.
11. The somiti's funds will initially be kept in a joint bank account, and a separate bank account in the somiti's name will be opened later as needed.
12. Decisions on government registration, bank accounts and applicable tax will be taken with the agreement of all members.
13. The rules for accepting, suspending or cancelling membership will be set with the agreement of all members.
14. A member who leaves the somiti voluntarily will allow the somiti 3 to 6 months to take back the money due to them. Within this time the somiti will pay the money due according to the rules. However, a member who leaves before the final profit distribution will not be entitled to any share of the profit.
15. If a member cancels membership while an investment or project is ongoing, they cannot claim a share of profit earned from that investment or project in the future.
16. After membership is cancelled or the somiti is left, the accounts will be finalised and the money due will be paid to the member or the nominated nominee within 3 to 6 months at most.
17. If the somiti's money is invested and that investment yields regular profit or dividend, a member who cancels membership will be paid, along with their deposited money, up to 6 months of profit or dividend from that investment according to their shares.
18. If a member dies, their family may continue the membership if they wish. If they wish to cancel the membership instead, the accounts will be finalised and the money due will be paid to the nominee or the family within 3 to 6 months at most.
19. Every member is bound to follow the somiti's fixed rules, decisions and discipline.
20. If a member breaks the somiti's rules, a fine or a fixed penalty will be imposed according to the decision of all, after discussion with all the other members, and that member is bound to accept it.
21. Important financial, investment and administrative decisions of the somiti will be taken based on the opinion and agreement of all members.
22. The agreement of all members must be obtained to change, add or cancel any rule of the somiti.
23. The method of distributing the somiti's profit will be set with the agreement of all members.
24. No profit money will be paid to any member before the final profit calculation is complete.
